| 250 - 280 | 0.120 - 0.150 | 1.80 - 2.15 | 4.50 - 5.40 | - |
| 280 - 315 | 0.135 - 0.165 | 2.00 - 2.40 | 4.95 - 6.00 | - |
| 315 - 355 | 0.150 - 0.180 | 2.15 - 2.65 | 5.40 - 6.60 | - |
| 355 - 400 | 0.170 - 0.210 | 2.50 - 3.00 | 6.20 - 7.60 | - |
| 400 - 450 | 0.195 - 0.235 | 2.80 - 3.40 | 7.00 - 8.50 | - |
| 450 - 500 | 0.215 - 0.265 | 3.10 - 3.80 | 7.80 - 9.50 | - |
| 500 - 560 | 0.245 - 0.300 | 3.40 - 4.10 | 8.40 - 10.30 | - |
| 560 - 630 | 0.275 - 0.340 | 3.80 - 4.65 | 9.50 - 11.60 | - |

The full card runs to 1 800 mm bore. Bores above 630 mm are normally mounted with hydraulic nuts and the SKF Drive-up Method; see the full card in the [SKF drive-up reference card](/article/skf-drive-up-card).

## Same data in inches, with unmounted and residual clearance (Schaeffler/FAG J4592)

Useful when your feeler set is inch. **Smallest clearance after mounting** is the pass/fail check in Step 4.

| Bore (mm) over - incl. | Unmounted clearance CN | Unmounted clearance C3 | Unmounted clearance C4 | Reduction (in) | Drive-up on adapter sleeve (in), 1:12 | Min. residual clearance CN / C3 / C4 (in) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 24 - 30 | .0012 - .0018 | .0018 - .0022 | .0022 - .0029 | .0006 - .0008 | .012 - .016 | .0006 / .0008 / .0014 |
| 30 - 40 | .0014 - .0020 | .0020 - .0026 | .0026 - .0034 | .0008 - .0010 | .014 - .018 | .0006 / .0010 / .0016 |
| 40 - 50 | .0018 - .0024 | .0024 - .0032 | .0032 - .0039 | .0010 - .0012 | .018 - .020 | .0008 / .0012 / .0020 |
| 50 - 65 | .0022 - .0030 | .0030 - .0037 | .0037 - .0047 | .0012 - .0016 | .020 - .028 | .0010 / .0014 / .0022 |
| 65 - 80 | .0028 - .0037 | .0037 - .0047 | .0047 - .0059 | .0016 - .0020 | .028 - .033 | .0010 / .0016 / .0028 |
| 80 - 100 | .0032 - .0043 | .0043 - .0055 | .0055 - .0071 | .0018 - .0024 | .030 - .039 | .0014 / .0020 / .0031 |
| 100 - 120 | .0039 - .0053 | .0053 - .0067 | .0067 - .0087 | .0020 - .0028 | .031 - .047 | .0020 / .0026 / .0039 |
| 120 - 140 | .0047 - .0063 | .0063 - .0079 | .0079 - .0102 | .0026 - .0035 | .047 - .059 | .0022 / .0031 / .0043 |
| 140 - 160 | .0051 - .0071 | .0071 - .0091 | .0091 - .0118 | .0030 - .0039 | .051 - .067 | .0022 / .0035 / .0051 |
| 160 - 180 | .0055 - .0079 | .0079 - .0102 | .0102 - .0134 | .0031 - .0043 | .055 - .075 | .0024 / .0039 / .0059 |
| 180 - 200 | .0063 - .0087 | .0087 - .0114 | .0114 - .0146 | .0035 - .0051 | .059 - .087 | .0028 / .0039 / .0063 |
| 200 - 225 | .0071 - .0098 | .0098 - .0126 | .0126 - .0161 | .0039 - .0055 | .067 - .094 | .0031 / .0047 / .0071 |
| 225 - 250 | .0079 - .0106 | .0106 - .0138 | .0138 - .0177 | .0043 - .0059 | .071 - .102 | .0035 / .0051 / .0079 |
| 250 - 280 | .0087 - .0118 | .0118 - .0154 | .0154 - .0193 | .0047 - .0067 | .079 - .114 | .0039 / .0055 / .0087 |
| 280 - 315 | .0095 - .0130 | .0130 - .0169 | .0169 - .0213 | .0051 - .0075 | .087 - .126 | .0043 / .0059 / .0094 |

The minimum drive-up applies when the bearing's starting clearance is in the lower half of its band; the maximum when it is in the upper half. SKF and FAG values differ slightly because the tables were built from each maker's own bearing geometry. **Use the card that matches the bearing brand in your hand**, and when in doubt use the feeler gauge, not the nut angle.

## Worked example

Bearing **22222 EK C3** on a **H 322** sleeve, 100 mm shaft (bearing bore 110 mm, band 100-120).

| Step | Reading |
|---|---|
| Unmounted clearance measured at top rollers | 0.15 mm (inside C3 band of 0.135-0.170 for this size) |
| Target reduction from SKF card (100-120 mm) | 0.050 - 0.060 mm |
| Target mounted clearance | 0.15 - 0.055 = **about 0.095 mm** |
| Minimum permitted residual (C3, 100-120) | 0.065 mm (.0026") |
| Result | 0.095 mm ≥ 0.065 mm → **pass** |

## Common mistakes

- **Measuring the bottom rollers.** Clearance shows at the *unloaded* row position. With the bearing standing on the bench that is the top.
- **Washing out the factory oil**, then measuring "dry". Readings change.
- **Driving up by feel.** A 100 mm bearing gets ruined by a strong arm on a long spanner. Measure.
- **Backing off the nut a full tab** to get the washer to line up. Re-drive instead.
- **Forgetting the bearing walks along the shaft** as it is driven up. Position the sleeve so the *final* bearing centre lands in the housing centre.
- **Using a C3 card value on a Normal-clearance bearing.** The reduction value is the same; the residual minimum is not.$mw$, $mw$procedure$mw$, (select id from public.mw_categories where slug = $mw$bearings$mw$),
